@startuml setup_protocol_development
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
title Setup Protocol Development View

box "Peer i" #AliceBlue
actor User_i as User #LightCyan
participant Phone_i as Phone #CadetBlue
participant Iso_i as Iso #LightBlue
participant Boomlet_i as Boomlet #LightPink
participant ST_i as ST #Violet
participant Boomletwo_i as Boomletwo #LightGray
participant Niso_i as Niso #LightGreen
end box
participant Other_Peers as Peers #White
participant WT #Red
participant SAR_i as SAR #Yellow

autonumber "<b>[S00]"

note over User, SAR
  <b>Scope</b>
  One peer is expanded. Peer agreement and checkpoint exchanges run for all five peers.
  Guard definitions and detailed-message coverage are in setup_development_contracts.md.
  Exact schemas, cryptographic contexts, and failure classes are normative in ../../spec/SPEC.md.
end note

note over Boomlet #LightYellow
  <b>Boomlet setup states</b>
  EMPTY -> INSTALLED -> ST_ENROLLED -> PARAMS_REVIEWED -> PARAMETERS_AGREED
  -> WT_READY -> SAR_READY -> BACKUP_READY
end note

group SAR registration
User -> Phone: S-SAR-1  doxing_password, selected SarId, rescue data
note over Phone #LavenderBlush
  Derive SAR-specific doxing key and lookup identifier.
  Encrypt static data under the SAR root; dynamic bytes under device-derived keys.
end note
Phone -> SAR: S-SAR-2  doxing_data_identifier
SAR --> Phone: S-SAR-3  payment info; SAR records doxing_data_identifier, PROTOCOL_VERSION, and invoice
Phone --> User: S-SAR-4  payment info
User -> Phone: S-SAR-5  payment receipt
Phone -> SAR: S-SAR-6  payment receipts, doxing_data_identifier, static envelope, dynamic_update_auth_key, first_dynamic_doxing_data_upload
note over SAR #Pink: G-SAR-REGISTRATION
SAR --> Phone: S-SAR-7  signed DynamicRescueReceipt
note over Phone #Pink: Verify signed receipt under SPEC 10
Phone --> User: S-SAR-8  SAR registration confirmed
end

group Boomlet installation and consent enrollment
User -> Iso: S-INSTALL-1  network, key path inputs, entropy, passphrase, doxing password, SarId
note over Iso #Lavender: Derive mnemonic, normal key, and doxing key
Iso -> Boomlet: S-INSTALL-2  normal_pubkey_i, doxing_key, SarId
note over Boomlet #Lavender
  Generate Boomlet identity key and MuSig2 share.
  Validate the aggregate boom key.
  EMPTY -> INSTALLED
end note
Boomlet --> Iso: S-INSTALL-3  boomlet_identity_pubkey_i
Iso -> ST: S-PAIR-1  pair with boomlet_identity_pubkey_i
ST --> Iso: S-PAIR-2  st_identity_pubkey_i
Iso -> Boomlet: S-PAIR-3  st_identity_pubkey_i

loop S-CONSENT  exactly two fresh nonce-bound enrollment rounds
  Boomlet -> ST: Enc_ST(DuressChallenge{permutation[1..193], nonce}) via Iso
  ST -> User: five independently shuffled display columns
  User -> ST: one selection from each column
  ST -> Boomlet: Enc_Boomlet(DuressResponse{five original indices, nonce}) via Iso
  note over Boomlet #Pink
    Accept under G-SETUP-CONSENT-RESPONSE.
    Store the first resolved set; require the second resolved set to equal it.
  end note
end
note over Boomlet #Lavender: INSTALLED -> ST_ENROLLED
Iso --> User: S-INSTALL-4  mnemonic
end

group Setup instance review and peer agreement
User -> Niso: S-PARAMS-1  network and RPC configuration
Niso -> Boomlet: S-PARAMS-2  initialize peer setup
Boomlet --> Niso: S-PARAMS-3  Tor secret and Sig_Boomlet(PeerSetupRecord_i)
note over Niso #Pink: Accept local record under G-LOCAL-PEER-RECORD
Niso -> ST: S-PARAMS-4  signed local PeerSetupRecord_i
ST --> User: S-PARAMS-5  trusted display of local record
User <-> Peers: S-PARAMS-6  exchange five signed PeerSetupRecords out of band
User -> Niso: S-PARAMS-7  five records, ordered WT preferences, milestone blocks
Niso -> Boomlet: S-PARAMS-8  canonically ordered setup seed
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Accept under G-SETUP-SEED.
  Derive setup_instance_id from PROTOCOL_VERSION and the canonical seed.
end note
Boomlet --> Niso: S-REVIEW-1  setup_instance_id and Enc_ST(nonce-bound setup commitment)
Niso -> ST: S-REVIEW-2  commitment and canonical seed fields
note over ST #Pink: Accept under G-PARAMS-REVIEW
ST -> User: S-REVIEW-3  ordered peers, WT preferences, milestones, protocol version
User -> ST: S-REVIEW-4  approve exact displayed setup
ST -> Boomlet: S-REVIEW-5  Enc_Boomlet(Sig_ST(exact nonce-bound commitment)) via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink: Accept under G-PARAMS-REVIEW-APPROVAL; ST_ENROLLED -> PARAMS_REVIEWED

Boomlet -> Peers: S-AGREE-1  Sig_Boomlet(boomerang_params_fingerprint) via Niso
Peers --> Boomlet: S-AGREE-2  one matching signed fingerprint from every other peer via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Accept under G-SETUP-AGREEMENT.
  PARAMS_REVIEWED -> PARAMETERS_AGREED.
  C_parameters := checkpoint(setup_instance_id, parameters_agreed, zero)
end note
end

group WT activation and checkpoint synchronization
Boomlet -> WT: S-WT-1  setup_instance_id, signed PeerSetupRecord_i, signed params fingerprint via Niso
Peers -> WT: S-WT-2  corresponding registration from every other peer
note over WT #Pink: Accept all five registrations under G-WT-REGISTRATION
WT --> User: S-WT-3  peer-specific payment info bound to setup_instance_id via Niso
User -> WT: S-WT-4  payment receipt via Niso
WT --> Boomlet: S-WT-5  Sig_WT(WtSetupReceipt) via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink: Accept local receipt under G-WT-SETUP-RECEIPT
note over Boomlet #Lavender: C_wt := checkpoint(setup_instance_id, wt_ready, C_parameters)
Boomlet -> Peers: S-WT-6  Sig_Boomlet(C_wt) via Niso
Peers --> Boomlet: S-WT-7  matching Sig_Boomlet_j(C_wt) from every other peer via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Accept the local signature and four peer signatures under G-SETUP-CHECKPOINT.
  PARAMETERS_AGREED -> WT_READY
end note
end

group SAR activation and checkpoint synchronization
Boomlet -> WT: S-SAR-ACT-1  signed selected SarId and Enc_SAR(setup_instance_id, identifier) via Niso
note over WT #Pink: Accept binding under G-SAR-BINDING; select only the setup-bound SAR
WT -> SAR: S-SAR-ACT-2  encrypted identifier payload, Boomlet identity, setup_instance_id
SAR --> WT: S-SAR-ACT-3  Enc_Boomlet(Sig_SAR(SarSetupResponse))
WT --> Boomlet: S-SAR-ACT-4  Sig_WT(wrapper with exact SAR response) via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink: Accept WT wrapper and local SAR response under G-SAR-SETUP-RESPONSE
note over Boomlet #Lavender: C_sar := checkpoint(setup_instance_id, sar_ready, C_wt)
Boomlet -> Peers: S-SAR-ACT-5  Sig_Boomlet(C_sar) via Niso
Peers --> Boomlet: S-SAR-ACT-6  matching Sig_Boomlet_j(C_sar) from every other peer via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Accept the local signature and four peer signatures under G-SETUP-CHECKPOINT.
  WT_READY -> SAR_READY
end note
end

group Backup activation and final checkpoint
User -> Iso: S-BACKUP-1  install empty Boomletwo and provide recovery inputs
Iso -> Boomletwo: S-BACKUP-2  initialize target
Boomletwo --> Iso: S-BACKUP-3  boomletwo_identity_pubkey
Iso -> Boomlet: S-BACKUP-4  Sig_normal(BoomletBackupRequest{target key, normal pubkey})
note over Boomlet #Pink: Accept once under G-BACKUP-REQUEST
Boomlet --> Iso: S-BACKUP-5  target-encrypted backup state, boomerang_params, signed SAR response
note over Iso #Pink
  Accept under G-BACKUP-PACKAGE.
  Reconstruct descriptor; verify active identity, milestones, SAR response, and static-data commitment.
end note
Iso -> Boomletwo: S-BACKUP-6  active identity and target-encrypted backup state
note over Boomletwo #Pink: Require empty target; authenticate, decrypt, and import state with embedded setup_instance_id
Boomletwo --> Iso: S-BACKUP-7  Sig_Boomletwo(BackupDone)
Iso -> Boomlet: S-BACKUP-8  Sig_Boomletwo(BackupDone)
note over Boomlet #Pink: Accept under G-BACKUP-DONE; mark backup complete
note over Boomlet #Lavender: C_backup := checkpoint(setup_instance_id, backup_ready, C_sar)
Boomlet -> Peers: S-BACKUP-9  Sig_Boomlet(C_backup) via Niso
Peers --> Boomlet: S-BACKUP-10  matching Sig_Boomlet_j(C_backup) from every other peer via Niso
note over Boomlet #Pink
  Accept the local signature and four peer signatures under G-SETUP-CHECKPOINT.
  SAR_READY -> BACKUP_READY; persist final checkpoint before success.
end note
Boomlet --> User: S-DONE  setup complete via Niso
end

note over User, SAR #LightYellow
  Any invalid identity, signature, envelope, nonce, setup binding, ordering, receipt, checkpoint,
  or state transition stalls the attempt under the failure rules in SPEC section 18.
end note

@enduml
